Records: {
	# Reforged pots
	CoinPortal:
		'''
		Always contains a coin portal.

		A lucky find!
		'''
	Common:
		'''
		A common pot which sometimes contains useful goodies.

		Value increases when further underground.
		'''
	Zenith:
		'''
		A common pot which sometimes contains useful goodies... this one is needlessly gaudy.

		Value increases when further underground.
		'''
	Potion: Contains a potent brew.
	UpsideDown: `Manufacturing error`
	Worm: Scatters a variety of worms when destroyed.
	Platter: A hot meal ready for the taking. Who would leave this behind?
	WickerBasket: A picnic, just for you!
	Aether: Provides various useful, sparkly upgrades.
	Stuffed: What a strange place to find a merchant. They're just asking to be bothered.
	Scrying: Reveals a large portion of the map upon being destroyed.
	Biome: Contains a greater variety of loot than common pots.
	Boulder: Rolls along the ground when disturbed.
	Wax: Imbued with potent magical energies.

	# Spooky cross mod pots
	SpookyForest: {
		Name: Stuffed Pail
		Entry: The leading edge of flimsy candy carriers.
	}

	SpiderGrotto: {
		Name: Webbed Cooking Pot
		Entry: ...who cooked all of these?
	}

	NoseTemple: {
		Name: Porcelain Nose
		Entry: The fanciest porcelain for the haughtiest noses.
	}

	FetidFarms: {
		Name: Groceries
		Entry: Fresh grown produce!
	}

	RottenDepths: {
		Name: Loaded Skeletons
		Entry: Seems like these fish swallowed some goods.
	}

	TarPits: {
		Name: Taramic Pot
		Entry: Ornate, slightly sticky, kinda cracked.
	}

	Krampus: {
		Name: Awesome Present
		Entry: The coolest gift boxes you've ever seen.
	}

	UpperCatacombs: {
		Name: Ancient Carved Pot
		Entry: The carvings on these are lovely, but hard to see.
	}

	LowerCatacombs: {
		Name: Jeering Pot
		Entry: They sneer at you.
	}
}

